    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit log confirms the new format: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, dropping sequence numbers entirely. Each piece of logic stayed in the unit that owns it:\n\n**`CustomerCodeGenerator`** (`service/`) \u2014 now builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from a region plus the identity inputs. It computes `HASH8` as the first 8 upper-case hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The old city/last-name-prefix + sequence formatting is gone.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 no longer counts owners for a per-city sequence. It derives the region via the existing `Locality.forOwner(owner)` (postcode-preferred, city fallback) and passes the owner's already-normalized telephone and last name to the generator. `countOwnersInCity` remains for the city-capacity rule that still needs it.\n\n**`Locality`** (`model/`) \u2014 gained `fromCustomerCode(...)`, which reads the leading `<REGION>` segment out of the identity string.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping now derives from the region-and-hash identity via `Locality.fromCustomerCode(owner.getCustomerCode())`, falling back to `Locality.forOwner` only for owners that don't have a code yet (e.g. seed data). The membership-number docstring example was updated to the new form.\n\nThe values *built from* the `customerCode` needed no logic changes \u2014 they already read it, so they now automatically reflect the new identity:\n- **Membership number** (`OwnerMapper.formatMembershipNumber`) \u2192 `NSW-A1B2C3D4-M26`\n- **Check digit** (`CheckDigit.forOwner`) \u2192 Luhn over the digits of the new code\n- **Create audit record** (`OwnerAuditLogger`) \u2192 logs the new `customerCode`\n\nThe `customer_code` column (`VARCHAR(20)`) comfortably holds the new codes (max `UNKNOWN-XXXXXXXX` = 16 chars).",
